8986:     "Read directly in src/observe.rs. Recursive mode: the Search entry's `output` is `String::new()`, and the per-file entries are collected into `by_file: BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>>` keyed by filename, so grep's stdout order — the order a bound would consume — is not in the ledger. Two instruments by one argument value: `args.push("-r")` runs only inside `if root_path.is_dir()`, and `Exclusions::decide` (observe.rs:240-259) returns `Exclusions::None { why: "the caller named one file" }` for any non-directory root, verbatim. In single-file mode `-H` is pushed unconditionally so every line is `{file}:{lineno}:{text}` and `split_once(':')` yields one constant key, hence exactly one by_file entry whose Vec holds every matched line as `{lineno}:{text}` in stdout order, shipped as `output: matches.join("\n")` under `label: format!("{file} (grep: {pattern})")` — file, order and every matched line all in the ledger, so the full stdout reconstructs from that one entry. For look_path, `PendingEntry { output: shown, .. }` receives the complete selection."
