C27 is true as written, but it calls this case "degenerate" and the memo places it in a paragraph headed "a fifth case is degenerate rather than exempt", leaving the spelling to the implementer. Measured (F1), the whole-search label is not a corner: it carries 113 of tet61's 218, 51 of tet47's 127 and 38 of tet56's 145 machine-local path occurrences — more than the plain file labels in two of the three memos. What C27 undersells is that the label's difficulty is not only the empty-string root: the `search`/`no-match` exclusion note enumerates in-repo skipped paths in full absolute form, so relativizing the leading root alone leaves most of the occurrences in place. Whatever the implementer chooses here decides more of TET-42's delivered benefit than the case the design actually specifies, so it belongs in the contract as a decision, not in the closing paragraph as a hazard.
